content.text:
I believe you. The repo already has strong evidence of a real model:

- authored `abilities` in content;
- compiled `_contentAbilities`;
- registered ability specs;
- the canonical item-ability pipeline;
- separate proc/effect topology.

We jumped onto the nearest convenient surface and added `displayValues`, which is probably exactly how the redesign layers accumulated.

The right next move is not inventing another schema. It’s tracing one ability end-to-end—probably Fishing Rod—and identifying:

1. the authoritative authored fields;
2. the compiled runtime representation;
3. the actual activation context;
4. the canonical timing resolver;
5. the display projection.

Then we should make the tooltip consume that existing model and remove the ad hoc additions where possible.

